    "question": "Madison makes 30 paper boats and sets them afloat. 20% are eaten by fish and Madison shoots two of the others with flaming arrows. How many boats are left?",
    "gold": "22",
    "answer": "First find the number of boats eaten by fish: 30 boats * 20% = <<30*20*.01=6>>6 boats\nThen subtract the two groups of boats that were destroyed from the original number to find the number left: 30 boats - 6 boats - 2 boats = <<30-6-2=22>>22 boats\n#### 22"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine how many paper boats Madison has left, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the number of boats eaten by fish.\n2. Subtract the number of boats eaten by fish from the total number of boats.\n3. Subtract the number of boats shot with flaming arrows from the remaining boats.\n\nLet's start with the first step:\n\n1. Madison makes 30 paper boats and 20% of them are eaten by fish.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Number of boats eaten by fish} = 30 \\times \\frac{20}{100} = 30 \\times 0.20 = 6\n   \\]\n\n2. Subtract the number of boats eaten by fish from the total number of boats.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Remaining boats after fish} = 30 - 6 = 24\n   \\]\n\n3. Madison shoots two of the remaining boats with flaming arrows.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Remaining boats after arrows} = 24 - 2 = 22\n   \\]\n\nSo, the number of boats left is \\(\\boxed{22}\\).",
